{"findings":[{"finding":"The spec says it overrides accepted assumption ASM-24 (Stripe card payments) and switches to staff recording payments by hand, which contradicts an assumption the human accepted.","reqId":"REQ-75","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Order emails always go to the 'Buyer who placed the order', with no rule for when that Buyer is deactivated or moved to another company (AC-16.4), so company A's order details could be emailed to a Fleet Co user.","reqId":"REQ-47","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"REQ-2 hides whether an account exists behind one identical 401, but REQ-3 returns 423 'locked' only for real accounts and AC-4.1 returns 403 'account is inactive', so either response reveals that the email is registered.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-25 prices every basket line from the price list current 'at the time of the request', yet REQ-42/AC-42.2 rejects submission because a line was 're-priced'; that only makes sense if the basket stores the price from when the line was added, which REQ-25 rules out.","reqId":"REQ-42","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-44 stores a copy of the delivery address on the order, but REQ-57 still refuses to confirm when the original address 'no longer exists', so staff removing an address (AC-82.3) blocks confirmation of every Received order that used it.","reqId":"REQ-82","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No requirement or acceptance criterion says what happens when a Buyer submits an empty basket, or one with no delivery address or no delivery date selected.","reqId":"REQ-44","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Staff may remove lines from a Received order, but nothing stops them removing the last line, which would leave an order with no lines that can still be confirmed and invoiced.","reqId":"REQ-55","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Confirmation checks stock, retired products and the address, but not whether the requested delivery date has already passed or is no longer valid (for example after a settings change).","reqId":"REQ-57","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No behaviour is defined for retiring a category that still has active products: are they hidden, uncategorised or still shown under the filter, and is retiring blocked?","reqId":"REQ-77","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Deactivating a price list that is assigned to companies has no acceptance criterion or error path, even though, per the spec's assumption, every product for those companies becomes 'Price on request' and ordering stops.","reqId":"REQ-28","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Invitations have no error path for an email that already belongs to an existing account, or for inviting a Buyer into an inactive company.","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Admins can change roles and deactivate users, but nothing stops them demoting or deactivating the last remaining Administrator, including themselves.","reqId":"REQ-18","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Password reset and invitation acceptance set no password rules (rejecting empty or weak passwords) and do not say whether the user's other sessions are ended after a reset.","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Nothing says whether a password reset works for a Pending (invited) account, which could let someone activate it without the invitation link, or for a deactivated account.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"There is no way to reverse or correct an invoice marked paid by mistake; once Paid, every further action returns 409 ALREADY_PAID.","reqId":"REQ-75","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"A repeated order merging into a basket that already holds the same product has no rule for adding the quantities together and capping the total at stock.","reqId":"REQ-52","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Changing a Buyer's company (AC-16.4) does not say what happens to their open session's basket (priced from the old company's list, possibly with the old company's address) or to their past orders.","reqId":"REQ-16","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-3.4 checks that 'the account record lock field is empty', which is internal storage and not visible through any API response.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-28.1 and AC-28.3 check database 'row' counts on the price list rather than an API response; AC-80.1 ('company row') and AC-61.2 ('order row stores the reason') do the same.","reqId":"REQ-28","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-35.1 depends on recording network traffic to 'the ERP host', which no public endpoint exposes, and it clashes with reading the file over SFTP (ASM-7) if the ERP host is the file location.","reqId":"REQ-35","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Import rows are matched on distributor product code and checked against fixed 'required columns', even though ASM-7 says the client will supply the column layout, so the column names and matching key should be configurable.","reqId":"REQ-31","rubric":8,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The spec fixes 'one currency with 2 decimal places' but the settings list in REQ-83 has no currency setting, so the currency shown on prices, invoices and PDFs is hardcoded and never named.","reqId":"REQ-83","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Dashboard counts of failed stock imports (REQ-67, REQ-69) are neither order queues nor delivery information (I-6), and these low-stability requirements add dashboard features beyond what was asked.","reqId":"REQ-67","rubric":4,"severity":"low"}],"note":"No OpenAI key: critic ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer)"}